\par
defined before developing the model. When the scenarios are defined afterwards, they
\par
may concern aspects that were not included in the model, making it difficult to address
\par
them without altering the structure of the model. Furthermore, when defining the
\par
scenarios the availability of data should be kept in mind. In the lung transplantation
\par
study, it would have been interesting to check whether cost-effectiveness is more
\par
favourable for certain patient groups. However, the small number of patients per group
\par
would have made the results highly unreliable.
