\par
known that activities, such as sampling, will result in some error but the magnitude of
\par
the error is uncertain. Therefore, trying to estimate the error prior to investigation is a
\par
way of handling the uncertainty. This explains way the two terms often are used as
\par
synonyms.
\par
Risk is often defined as a combination of the probability of a harmful event to occur and
\par
the loss (consequences) of the outcome of this event. However, there are numerous
\par
other definitions, which makes it necessary to clearly define the term ``risk'' in each ap-
\par
plication it is used to avoid misinterpretation.
