An advantage of Bayesian statistics compared to classical statistics is that all sources of
\par
information can be considered. This includes direct evidence from statistical sampling
\par
as well as indirect evidence of whatever kind available from past experience of the
\par
analyst or other experts (Hoffman and Kaplan, 1999).
