\par
the theory may still be incomplete. For quantification of the fundamental error one im-
\par
portant parameter is the maximum particle size of the medium. If the pollutants are
\par
heavy metals grinding will (probably) not alter the chemical composition but for volatile
\par
or semi-volatile chemicals this technique is inappropriate. However, most soils do not
\par
require grinding unless gravel, cobbles, or other large components are present (Mason,
\par
1992).
\par
The extension of the theory to volatile or semi-volatile chemicals is an undeveloped part
\par
of environmental sampling (Flatman and Yfantis, 1996). Further discussion on this
\par
matter can be found in Mason (1992).
