\textbf{3.2 Overview of Co-operative Decision Making}
\par
In decentralized computer systems, the \textbf{processors }often must collaborate to. solve a \textbf{particular }system or
\par
application problem. \textbf{The }problems may range from those associated with the management of system
\par
resources (such as deciding which processor should process a particular task) to those arising in a specific
\par
application such as speech recognition. We propose to try to deal with these problems in a general way \textbf{by}
\par
casting them in a framework of statistical decision theory. Once in such a framework, it is possible to consider
\par
issues such as the importance or value of information and its decline in value with time delays.
