A second consideration which often leads to decentralized decision making is the delay in and the cost of
\par
\textbf{*, }interprocess communication. In many real-time applications such as load balancing, information delay often
\par
\textbf{" }plays a dominant role, and rapid decision making may be crucial. \textbf{The }time delay incurred in collecting
