\par
impacts on a firm with varied levels of focus, it follows that a number of business value measures,
\par
rather than a single measure, should be developed to best inform management about the aspects
\par
of IT performance most relevant to the success of its strategy. Though unitary measures will con-
\par
tinue to be attractive and simple for managers to understand -- the net present value NPV of
\par
an IT investment is a good example -- it is unlikely that they will provide the robustness,
\par
validity, responsiveness, informativeness and transferability necessary to support powerful
\par
management insights into the effectiveness of IT investmenfs.
