In this paper we present a method to provide evidence for the linkage between specific infor-
\par
mation technology investments and "strategic" outputs which occur a t higher levels of an or-
\par
ganization. This method represents our response to the challenge of "filling the process box" em-
\par
bodied in the remarks of Crowston and Treacy. Advances in performance assessment for IT will
\par
result when indirect inputs and outputs are \emph{validated }as contributors to and results of a produc-
\par
tion process. Our approach to determining which inputs and outputs are relevant develops a
