\par
linked to ATM deployment. The manager's belief that retail payment IT produces business value
\par
for the bank can be reduced to a hypothesis testable via our BVL regression approach. Such a test
\par
involves identifying the role that various independent variables might have in the creation of
\par
demand deposit or savings deposit dollars, the dependent variable in this case. The independent
\par
variables used to predict area deposits might include local demographic factors and branch design
\par
characteristics, including the presence of ATM, the network the banks participates in, the number
\par
of ATMs in the competing network, its relevant rates of in:erest, and so on.
